CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] file main.sh line 4 assertion "\$\{\?\}" -eq 0: FAILURE$
^\[assertion\.2\] file main.sh line 6 assertion "\$\{\?\}" -eq 0: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Opening a file for a redirection can fail. The command is then skipped
with a non-zero status, and dash exits if the command is a special
builtin such as ":" (XCU 2.8.1), so the second assertion holds.
